From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:54:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build: link LTO with mold on one thread

mold calls the LTO plugin for its input files from several threads, so
the order in which GCC's whole-program optimization gets them changes
from one link to the next, and with it what LTO decides: linking
jansson's library six times from the same objects gave six different
libraries, and GCC warned of an overflow in some links and not in the
others. With one thread every link gave the same library, as with
ld.bfd.

Link with mold on one thread when the package uses LTO. The link of an
LTO package is GCC's work almost entirely; other links keep mold's
threads.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 include/package.mk | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/package.mk b/include/package.mk
index c187ac0..ecccb80 100644
--- a/include/package.mk
+++ b/include/package.mk
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@ endif
 ifdef CONFIG_USE_MOLD
   ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,mold,1),1)
     TARGET_LINKER:=mold
+    # mold hands the LTO plugin its input files from several threads, in an
+    # order that varies from link to link, and the code LTO makes with it.
+    ifneq ($(filter -flto%,$(TARGET_LDFLAGS)),)
+      TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -Wl,--threads=1
+    endif
   endif
 endif
 
